      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T18:29:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, the version check pinned nothing the require() didn\u0027t already. Replaced it in PS5.\n\nprocess.execPath doesn\u0027t resolve under runfiles, though. It\u0027s the resolved binary, and the runfiles entry symlinks out to wherever Bazel fetched Node. Locally that\u0027s the repository cache (~/.gerritcodereview/bazel-cache/repository/contents/...), so an under-runfiles assertion fails on a correct setup.\n\nThe test now asserts that realpath(execPath) differs from every `node` reachable via PATH. If no system node exists, a launcher that fell back to a bare `node` wouldn\u0027t start at all, so both cases fail. I checked that the assertion fires by putting a symlink to the toolchain binary first on PATH (--test_env\u003dPATH\u003d...).",
